{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed stitch task (#5106) to implement three functions in `pkg/hashutil` for the go-unix-utils project: `ParseChecksumLine` (parse GNU and BSD tag checksum formats), `VerifyChecksums` (read checksum file, verify entries, print OK/FAILED results respecting CheckOptions), and `DigestFiles` (compute and print digests for file lists, supporting stdin via '-'). These implement srd086-hashutil requirements R3.1 and R3.2. The task is part of an automated code generation pipeline where git is managed externally.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU checksum format: `HASH  FILENAME` (text mode, two spaces) or `HASH *FILENAME` (binary mode, space+asterisk)\n   - BSD tag checksum format: `ALGORITHM (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - CheckOptions: Warn (print warnings for malformed lines), Quiet (suppress OK lines), Status (suppress all output, exit code only)\n   - Regex-based line parsing for both formats\n   - io.ReadCloser pattern with io.NopCloser for stdin handling\n   - 40-line function limit (E8 constitution rule)\n   - No git commands allowed - managed externally by orchestrator\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd086-hashutil.yaml`\n     - Read to understand the full SRD specification\n     - Defines HashConfig, CheckOptions, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles contracts\n     - Key: R2.1 (ParseChecksumLine), R2.3 (VerifyChecksums), R3.1 (DigestFiles), R3.2 (continue on file errors)\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashconfig.go` (MODIFIED)\n     - Contains types (HashConfig, CheckOptions) and formatting functions (FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest)\n     - Removed three stub functions to avoid duplicate definitions when creating hashutil.go\n     - Current state after edit (lines 1-55):\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     // Package hashutil provides shared hash output formatting and checksum\n     // verification logic for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum, sha224sum,\n     // sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, and sum utilities.\n     // Implements srd086-hashutil R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4.\n     package hashutil\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"encoding/hex\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"hash\"\n     \t\"io\"\n     )\n     \n     type HashConfig struct {\n     \tAlgorithm string\n     \tNewHash   func() hash.Hash\n     \tDigestLen int\n     }\n     \n     type CheckOptions struct {\n     \tWarn   bool\n     \tQuiet  bool\n     \tStatus bool\n     }\n     \n     func FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string {\n     \tif binary {\n     \t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s *%s\", digest, filename)\n     \t}\n     \treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s  %s\", digest, filename)\n     }\n     \n     func FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string {\n     \treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s) = %s\", algorithm, filename, digest)\n     }\n     \n     func ComputeDigest(r io.Reader, cfg HashConfig) (string, error) {\n     \th := cfg.NewHash()\n     \tif _, err := io.Copy(h, r); err != nil {\n     \t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"computing digest: %w\", err)\n     \t}\n     \treturn hex.EncodeToString(h.Sum(nil)), nil\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go` (NEEDS TO BE CREATED)\n     - Does not exist yet - this is the primary deliverable\n     - Planned implementation with these functions and helpers:\n     ```go\n     // Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n     // SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n     \n     package hashutil\n     \n     import (\n     \t\"bufio\"\n     \t\"fmt\"\n     \t\"io\"\n     \t\"os\"\n     \t\"regexp\"\n     )\n     \n     var (\n     \tbsdTagRe = regexp.MustCompile(`^(\\S+) \\((.+)\\) = ([0-9a-fA-F]+)\n\n)\n     \tgnuRe    = regexp.MustCompile(`^([0-9a-fA-F]+) ([ *])(.+)\n\n)\n     )\n     \n     func ParseChecksumLine(line string, cfg HashConfig) (filename, expectedDigest string, binary bool, err error) {\n     \tif m := bsdTagRe.FindStringSubmatch(line); m != nil {\n     \t\treturn m[2], m[3], false, nil\n     \t}\n     \tif m := gnuRe.FindStringSubmatch(line); m != nil {\n     \t\treturn m[3], m[1], m[2] == \"*\", nil\n     \t}\n     \treturn \"\", \"\", false, fmt.Errorf(\"malformed checksum line\")\n     }\n     \n     func VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error) {\n     \tr, err := openInput(checksumFile)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"opening checksum file: %w\", err)\n     \t}\n     \tdefer r.Close()\n     \treturn verifyLines(r, cfg, opts, stdout, stderr)\n     }\n     \n     func verifyLines(r io.Reader, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error) {\n     \tscanner := bufio.NewScanner(r)\n     \tallOK := true\n     \tfor scanner.Scan() {\n     \t\tif !verifyOneLine(scanner.Text(), cfg, opts, stdout, stderr) {\n     \t\t\tallOK = false\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \tif err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {\n     \t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"reading checksum input: %w\", err)\n     \t}\n     \treturn allOK, nil\n     }\n     \n     func verifyOneLine(line string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) bool {\n     \tfilename, expected, _, err := ParseChecksumLine(line, cfg)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tif opts.Warn && !opts.Status {\n     \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"WARNING: improperly formatted checksum line\\n\")\n     \t\t}\n     \t\treturn true\n     \t}\n     \tactual, err := computeFileDigest(filename, cfg)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\tif !opts.Status {\n     \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"%s: FAILED open or read\\n\", filename)\n     \t\t}\n     \t\treturn false\n     \t}\n     \tif actual != expected {\n     \t\tif !opts.Status {\n     \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"%s: FAILED\\n\", filename)\n     \t\t}\n     \t\treturn false\n     \t}\n     \tif !opts.Status && !opts.Quiet {\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintf(stdout, \"%s: OK\\n\", filename)\n     \t}\n     \treturn true\n     }\n     \n     func computeFileDigest(filename string, cfg HashConfig) (string, error) {\n     \tf, err := os.Open(filename)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn \"\", err\n     \t}\n     \tdefer f.Close()\n     \treturn ComputeDigest(f, cfg)\n     }\n     \n     func DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n     \tif len(files) == 0 {\n     \t\tfiles = []string{\"-\"}\n     \t}\n     \texitCode := 0\n     \tfor _, file := range files {\n     \t\tif err := digestAndPrint(file, cfg, binary, tag, stdout); err != nil {\n     \t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(stderr, \"%s: %s\\n\", file, err)\n     \t\t\texitCode = 1\n     \t\t}\n     \t}\n     \treturn exitCode\n     }\n     \n     func digestAndPrint(file string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout io.Writer) error {\n     \tr, err := openInput(file)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn err\n     \t}\n     \tdefer r.Close()\n     \tdigest, err := ComputeDigest(r, cfg)\n     \tif err != nil {\n     \t\treturn err\n     \t}\n     \tif tag {\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintln(stdout, FormatBSDTag(cfg.Algorithm, file, digest))\n     \t} else {\n     \t\tfmt.Fprintln(stdout, FormatGNU(digest, file, binary))\n     \t}\n     \treturn nil\n     }\n     \n     func openInput(file string) (io.ReadCloser, error) {\n     \tif file == \"-\" {\n     \t\treturn io.NopCloser(os.Stdin), nil\n     \t}\n     \treturn os.Open(file)\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. The only action completed was removing stub functions from hashconfig.go. The new file has not been created 